;; global-legislation-datoms — hand-curated legal-source catalog.
;;
;; Every row is a *catalog* entry (jurisdiction × source × license × sensor
;; readiness), NOT ingested full text. Grounded exclusively in facts already
;; on record elsewhere in the com-junkawasaki monorepo, or (for license
;; grading only, see below) in well-established black-letter copyright law:
;;
;; - :doc/adr-2605262800   — etzhayyim/root 90-docs/adr/2605262800-public-data-legal-corpus-ipfs-ingestion.md
;;                           (per-jurisdiction source list + Tier-A/B/C license grading)
;; - :doc/kotodama-py-legal-sensors-readme — kotoba-lang/kotodama-py
;;                           src/kotodama/organism/sensors/legal/README.md (wave-1 5-anchor table)
;; - :doc/hanrei-claude-md — etzhayyim/root 60-apps/etzhayyim-project-hanrei/AGENTS.md
;;                           (explicit e-Gov / kanpo / courts.go.jp URLs)
;; - :doc/hanrei-actor-manifest — etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-hanrei/actor-manifest.jsonld
;;                           (convoSystemPrompt: "83 jurisdictions ... 8 international
;;                           courts: ICJ/ICC/ECHR/CJEU/IACHR/ACHPR/ITLOS/WTO AB")
;;
;; :legal-source/url-provenance distinguishes a URL string that appears
;; verbatim in one of those docs (:doc-literal) from a well-known official
;; government-portal domain that is the obvious referent of a named source
;; but was not independently re-fetched here (:well-known-domain — consistent
;; with the passive-only, no-live-scrape invariant of ADR-2605262400 §7).
;;
;; :legal-source/license-provenance is the SAME distinction applied to
;; license grading. :doc-literal means the license string was quoted
;; verbatim from an in-repo doc (the 5 wave-1 anchors + fr-legifrance).
;; :general-legal-knowledge means the tier was assigned from well-established
;; copyright-law facts (a specific statute's public-works carve-out, or a
;; known org copyright policy) rather than an in-repo doc — every such row
;; carries :legal-source/license-basis citing the specific legal basis, so a
;; reader can independently verify or dispute the grading. This is a
;; materially weaker provenance claim than :doc-literal and MUST NOT be
;; conflated with it.
;;
;; :legal-source/status was :status/cataloged for every row without exception
;; until 2026-08-04. Per ADR-2605262800, R0 shipped only the ADR + sensor
;; scaffold + fetcher path-reserves, so this file was the pre-ingestion
;; registry and nothing more.
;;
;; That changed with ADR-2608041800: four sources now have their full text
;; preserved in locked DataLad datasets and carry :status/ingested plus a
;; :legal-source/dataset pointing at the repository that holds the bytes.
;; EVERY OTHER ROW IS STILL :status/cataloged, and the distinction is the
;; point -- "we know where this source is" and "we have this source" must
;; never read the same. Query :legal-source/status, not the row's existence.
;;
;; :legal-source/hanrei-court-code tags the 8 rows that correspond 1:1 to
;; hanrei's own "8 international courts" list (ICJ/ICC/ECHR/CJEU/IACHR/
;; ACHPR/ITLOS/WTO AB per :doc/hanrei-actor-manifest), so a query can confirm
;; full coverage of that specific set independent of this catalog's own ids.

